1
00:00:05,081 --> 00:00:07,291
(Sheldon:)Stop yelling.

2
00:00:07,917 --> 00:00:09,587
(Sheldon:)I'm not happy about this.

3
00:00:09,752 --> 00:00:12,592
(Leonard:)What's the last thing
you were ever happy about?

4
00:00:12,797 --> 00:00:14,507
(Sheldon:)The prospect of fried chicken.

5
00:00:16,092 --> 00:00:18,092
(Mrs Cooper:)This is exciting.

6
00:00:18,303 --> 00:00:20,683
(Mrs Cooper:)Back home, the diner
on Route 4 serves sushi...

7
00:00:20,847 --> 00:00:24,017
(Mrs Cooper:)...but it's just cut up fish sticks
and a side of Uncle Ben's.

8
00:00:25,310 --> 00:00:30,190
(Mrs Cooper:)They put it on the menu in those kung fu
Ietters, but that don't make it sushi.

9
00:00:30,773 --> 00:00:34,943
Uh, "Kung fu letters"
might not be politically correct.

10
00:00:35,361 --> 00:00:38,401
(Mrs Cooper:)Oh, I thought the one
we couldn't say was "ching chong."

11
00:00:39,866 --> 00:00:41,866
(Leonard:)Yeah, yeah, that too.

12
00:00:42,452 --> 00:00:45,452
(Mrs Cooper:)So, Shelly, what's up with you
and your friend Amy...

13
00:00:45,622 --> 00:00:47,792
(Mrs Cooper:)...if you don't mind
a mother prying a bit?

14
00:00:47,957 --> 00:00:50,797
(Sheldon:)Well, there's actually big news
on the Amy front.

15
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:55,090
(Sheldon:)She's been studying the neurobiology
of addiction in lower animals.

16
00:00:55,256 --> 00:00:58,926
She's this close to getting a starfish
hooked on cocaine.

17
00:01:00,136 --> 00:01:02,476
(Mrs Cooper:)You have any idea
what's going on with those two?

